# Farq Construction UI (this repo = frontend only)
# Copy to .env.local — never commit secrets.
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Architecture (matches farq-tech/farq)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# EN: Browser → VITE_API_BASE_URL (/_api) → Farq Express /api/construction/*
#     Never put Postgres URLs in this frontend.
# AR: الواجهة فقط — لا تضع رابط Postgres هنا أبداً.
#
# ── Frontend (this repo) ───────────────────────────────────────
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/_api
VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:3000
# Real sign-in needs NOTHING here: the app posts email + password to
# /api/auth/login on the Farq API and holds the account's own session. That
# requires FARQ_AUTH_JWT_SECRET to be set on the API, or login answers 503.
#
# VITE_FARQ_ACCESS_TOKEN is a LOCAL DIAGNOSTIC ONLY and is ignored in
# production builds. One token baked into the bundle is a session shared by
# every visitor, which is the opposite of an account per person.
# VITE_FARQ_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# Or call production API directly (CORS must allow this origin):
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.farq.sa
# VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET=https://api.farq.sa

# ── Farq API / Railway ONLY (api/.env — NOT this frontend) ─────
#
# Required for live construction data:
#   CONSTRUCTION_DB_URL=${{Postgres.DATABASE_URL}}   # Railway farq-api-test-oregon
#   CONSTRUCTION_READ_ENABLED=1
#   CONSTRUCTION_WRITE_ENABLED=1   # create RFQ / award / projects
#   CONSTRUCTION_RFQ_ENABLED=1
#   CONSTRUCTION_ADAPTERS_ENABLED=1  # optional BOQ PDF parse helpers
#
# No-login local demo (NODE_ENV !== production):
#   CONSTRUCTION_DEMO_MODE=1
#   CONSTRUCTION_DEMO_BUYER_USER_ID=<uuid of buyer who owns RFQs>
#     → Farq api/lib/construction/runtime.js maps x-construction-demo-user
#       to this UUID (ADMIN). Without it, demo actor is a stable hash UUID
#       (empty RFQ list until you create one).
#
# Frontend sends: x-construction-demo-user: local-buyer
#
# Gmail OAuth (Farq API / Railway only — never VITE_ secrets):
#   CONSTRUCTION_GMAIL_ENABLED=1
#   CONSTRUCTION_GMAIL_SYNC_ENABLED=1   # optional read sync after connect
#   CONSTRUCTION_GMAIL_CLIENT_ID / CLIENT_SECRET / TOKEN_KEY
#   CONSTRUCTION_GMAIL_OWNER_ACTOR_ID=<same uuid as CONSTRUCTION_DEMO_BUYER_USER_ID for demo connect>
#   Optional: CONSTRUCTION_GMAIL_RETURN_TO_ORIGINS=preview.example.com,*.my-tunnel.dev
# Google Console authorized redirect URI (only this — not the Vite preview origin):
#   https://www.farq.sa/_api/api/construction/inbox/gmail/callback
# Connect from this UI uses launch_url on www.farq.sa then returns here with ?gmail=connected.
# For a real Google round-trip, proxy/target the production Farq API (same DB as that callback).
#
# Email / WhatsApp dispatch (award notifications + invite send):
#   CONSTRUCTION_RFQ_EMAIL_WEBHOOK_URL=...
#   CONSTRUCTION_RFQ_WHATSAPP_WEBHOOK_URL=...
#   RESEND_API_KEY=...
#   WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN / WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID / …
#
# ❌ Do NOT use: FARQ_DATABASE_URL, Vite→Postgres plugins, /api/farq/suppliers
#
# ── Production sign-in ─────────────────────────────────────────
# CONSTRUCTION_DEMO_MODE is ignored when NODE_ENV=production, so production
# runs on real accounts. On the Farq API set:
#   FARQ_AUTH_JWT_SECRET             — without it /api/auth/login answers 503
#   BUSINESS_NATIVE_INVITES_ENABLED=1 — to invite staff by email
# Rotating FARQ_AUTH_JWT_SECRET invalidates issued access tokens; the app
# recovers by refreshing once and, if refused, asking for the password again.
#
# Required Farq API patch for Postgres + no-login RFQs:
#   api/lib/construction/runtime.js — resolveDemoBuyerActorId + ADMIN demo role
#   (patched in /Users/m4pro/farq/api and /Volumes/Extreme SSD/farq/api)
